Iterator
---------

Iterator is an object used to traverse (visit) elements one by one from a collection.

Some collections - HashSet, TreeSet, Queue don't support indexing.
Iterator works with ALL collections. That's why Iterator is preferred than for loops

If we use for loop for modifying collection while looping it throws ConcurrentModificationException.
Whereas Iterator removes elements safely while modifying the collection while iteration.

Methods:
    hasNext() - Checks if another element exists
    next() - returns the next element
    remove() - removes the current element safely

Example: To remove inactive users from collection of users



